{%- comment -%}
The IG Publisher's package dependency table (`dependency-table.xhtml`, `-short`, `-nontech`), rendered by Jekyll from `site.data.fhir.dependencies`.
Called by the fragment `build-ig-site.ts` writes in place of the one the Publisher would have generated (bean `4475`), with `include.form`:
`full` (every row, nested by depth), `short` (the IG's own dependencies only) or `nontech` (titles only, as a list). Every value — the rows, their order,
their depth, whether the package cache held a package — is computed by `ig-dependencies.ts`; this file only arranges them. A package the cache did not
hold is SAID, rather than shown as a leaf that depends on nothing. No dependencies at all is said too.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign rows = site.data.fhir.dependencies -%}
{%- if rows and rows.size > 0 -%}
{%- if include.form == "nontech" %}
<ul class="ig-dependency-list">
{%- for r in rows %}{% if r.depth == 0 %}<li>{{ r.title | default: r.packageId | escape }}</li>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</ul>
{%- else %}
<table class="ig-dependency-table grid">
<thead><tr><th>IG</th><th>Package</th><th>FHIR</th><th>Comment</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for r in rows %}{% if include.form == "short" and r.depth > 0 %}{% continue %}{% endif %}
<tr class="ig-dependency-depth-{{ r.depth }}">
<td style="padding-left: {{ r.depth | times: 1.5 | plus: 0.25 }}em">{% if r.canonical %}<a href="{{ r.canonical }}">{{ r.title | default: r.packageId | escape }}</a>{% else %}{{ r.title | default: r.packageId | escape }}{% endif %}</td>
<td><a href="https://simplifier.net/packages/{{ r.packageId }}/{{ r.version }}">{{ r.packageId }}#{{ r.version }}</a></td>
<td>{{ r.fhirVersion }}</td>
<td>{% if r.repeat %}listed above{% elsif r.resolved == false %}not in the package cache this build read, so what it depends on is not shown{% endif %}</td>
</tr>
{%- endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{%- endif %}
{%- else %}
<p class="ig-dependency-table-empty">This guide declares no package dependencies.</p>
{%- endif %}
